## User preferences

- For software cleanup the user said “先给我一个可以删掉的程序的列表。我说可以删了，你就可以删了” -> audit read-only, present candidates and wait fo
r explicit confirmation before uninstalling; explain identities and dependencies in the list. [Task 1]
- When asking which programs “影响运行速度” distinguish installed size from startup entries, services, running processes and 
measured resource use. [Task 1]
- The user corrected “ESB Browser，ES Browser是那个Chrome浏览器，你把这个删了干嘛，给我装回去”; they first chose recovery, then “下载一个新的Chrome
浏览器吧” after it was blocked -> check the browser they actually use before removal; distinguish failed restoration from a
 user-selected replacement and preserve the old profile. [Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- Inventory uninstall registrations, AppX, services, Run entries, scheduled tasks, startup folders and process/resource
 samples. A short sample found roughly 0.9–1.2 GiB available of 16 GiB, CPU 14–34%, SSD queue 0: evidence of memory pre
ssure during that interval, not historical performance. Win工具箱 had five auto-running services; OneBrowser had an update
r. [Task 1]
- Protect development, scientific and system dependencies such as Conda/Python, Visual C++ runtimes, WebView2, Office, 
PostgreSQL, MiKTeX, Pandoc, Git, Node.js and VS Code unless their purpose and removal are confirmed. Verify removal ind
ependently through paths, registrations, processes, services, startup entries and tasks; exit codes alone are insuffici
ent. Backups still occupy disk space. [Task 1]
- `C:\Program Files\ESBrowser\ESBrowser.exe` was signed by Shihong (Xi'an) Internet Technology Co., Ltd., while `Google
 Chrome.lnk` and registered application name presented it as Google Chrome. Resolve shortcut targets and default-browse
r registrations, executable company/signature and user reliance before proposing removal; explain the identity and ask 
for specific confirmation. [Task 2]
- The original executable was found in a shadow copy with a matching recorded hash, but Defender quarantined it as `Tro
jan:Win32/Kepavll!rfn` (severe). Its profile at `C:\Users\李则徐\AppData\Local\ESBrowser\User Data` remained untouched. Th
e user then selected official Chrome; a Google LLC-signed enterprise MSI installed and launched successfully. The versi
on and installation state are historical. [Task 2]

## Failures and how to do differently

- A program's name, installed presence or registry-estimated size does not establish that it slows the PC or is safe to
 remove; duplicate Python, Visual C++ and AppX entries may represent distinct components. Check paths, active use and d
ependencies. [Task 1]
- Win工具箱's vendor uninstaller repeatedly spawned without a usable window; the original directory was backed up and five
 services removed, followed by independent checks. Treat this as a case-specific fallback, not a general license to rem
ove services or files. [Task 1]
- A browser shortcut named Google Chrome concealed ESBrowser -> map all user-facing aliases and registrations to the ac
tual executable and obtain identity-specific approval before uninstalling. [Task 2]
- A matching shadow-copy hash establishes identity, not safety; Defender blocked restoration, so do not bypass protecti
on or run the quarantined file. Google's standalone EXE crashed with `c0000005` / `-1073741819`; the official enterpris
e MSI worked in this instance. [Task 2]

